WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:09.676
Theo: Look at all the mud from the rain

2
00:00:09.677 --> 00:00:15.932
yesterday! Skyler: The wind blew down lots of

3
00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:18.593
branches. Miss Brook: Good

4
00:00:18.594 --> 00:00:22.801
morning, campers! Who's ready for another fun day?

5
00:00:22.802 --> 00:00:27.690
Riley: I hope the farm animals like us

6
00:00:27.691 --> 00:00:32.322
today. Ben: I hope Mack likes us

7
00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:35.164
today. Sarah: What's that

8
00:00:35.165 --> 00:00:39.203
noise? Theo: It sounds like

9
00:00:39.204 --> 00:00:44.431
a tractor. Miss Brook: It's Mack. The storm made

10
00:00:44.432 --> 00:00:47.132
a mess. So he's been busy all

11
00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:53.609
morning. Let's go see what he's doing. Kyle:

12
00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:59.977
Look! A tree fell by the pond!

13
00:00:59.978 --> 00:01:02.054
Miss Brook: Good morning, Mack.

14
00:01:02.055 --> 00:01:04.179
What are you doing? Mack:

15
00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:07.098
I have to move this tree. Theo:

16
00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:10.159
What will you do with it?

17
00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.816
Mack: I'll cut it up for firewood.

18
00:01:12.817 --> 00:01:16.666
Miss Brook: This looks like a big

19
00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:20.619
job. A huge branch fell in the pond! Mack:

20
00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:25.788
Uh-huh. I have to pull that out too.

21
00:01:25.789 --> 00:01:29.610
Riley: Hey, Ben, look at the branch!

22
00:01:29.611 --> 00:01:32.784
The little turtle is on it!

23
00:01:32.785 --> 00:01:35.551
Ben: It can bask in the sun now!

24
00:01:35.552 --> 00:01:39.721
Maybe Mack can leave the branch there.

25
00:01:39.722 --> 00:01:44.333
Ben: Um, Mack . . . Can the branch stay in the

26
00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:48.150
pond? That little turtle needs it for basking.

27
00:01:48.151 --> 00:01:51.890
There was no room on the rock yesterday.

28
00:01:51.891 --> 00:01:57.539
Mack: Huh. You kids really do care about animals.

29
00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:00.968
You showed that yesterday in the rain.

30
00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:03.449
I'll leave the branch in the pond. And

31
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:06.157
on the last day of camp . . . Ben:

32
00:02:06.158 --> 00:02:08.093
Yes? Mack:

33
00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:13.114
You can bring your pets—if they behave!

34
00:02:13.115 --> 00:02:19.857
Everyone: Yay!

